# WattGap needs no API keys: prices and load shapes are committed CSVs from ERCOT's public MIS (see data/PROVENANCE.md).

# Supervisor signing key: a 32-byte ed25519 seed as 64 hex characters. Batteries pin its public key.
# Each battery generates its own ed25519 keypair at enrollment; only public keys ever reach the supervisor.
# If unset, WattGap generates an ephemeral dev key at startup and logs a warning.
# Generate one with:  python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
WATTGAP_SUPERVISOR_KEY=replace-with-64-hex-chars
